OL,3,GNEWSAScot, 70, cross-stitched Bayeux
OL,4,ATapestry replica on his daily commute
OL,5,
OL,6,FA replica Bayeux Tapestry
OL,7,Fcross-stitched by an Aberdeenshire
OL,8,Fpensioner over nearly four decades is
OL,9,Fbeing put on display at the same time
OL,10,Fas the real thing in London.
OL,12,FThe work of Ian Williams, 70, is about
OL,13,Fa third of the size of the 230ft
OL,14,F(70m)-long original and will be on show
OL,15,Fat the Market Street Hall in Macduff.
OL,17,FThe actual Bayeux Tapestry has been
OL,18,Floaned to the British Museum by France
OL,19,Funtil July 2027 and is going on public
OL,20,Fdisplay in London for the first time.
OL,23,APub: 09-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB  Scot NewsC Reg TVF  Weather
